log x) with zero error (matches P1 / Thread 6 negative shape on the h-axis); APPROXIMATE regime per-h cost = Θ(polylog x) with ≤ 0.25 √x worst error (matches P3 / Thread 7 positive shape on the h-axis). **P2 is Thread-7 (P3) shape, NOT Thread-5 (S224) shape**: the cross-h amortisation in EXACT regime gives only a constant sieve-sharing factor (the h-axis is not a "correlation-of-x" axis in the relevant sense). **What this rules out**: (i) batched-sieve algorithm achieving o(x/log x) per-h amortised for any unbounded M family — directly tested at M ∈ {10..200} and ruled out; (ii) Thread-5-style cross-h correlation amortisation matching the 33× S224 speedup — does not materialise; (iii) the original P2 entry's "shared-h-singular-series structure" being interpreted as exact-cost amortisation — the shared structure helps only the polylog HL approximation, not the EXACT count. **What this does NOT close**: (i) non-sieve algorithms (GPY-weight / Maynard) for batched EXACT π_h — outside slot-1 scope; (ii) quantum batched (P9 shape); (iii) the precise named-exponent error bound for HL approximation — slot 2/3/4 candidate; (iv) the Q-truncation tradeoff for S_Q(h) → S_h — slot 3 candidate. **Pivoted A-grade target for slots 2-4**: precise named-exponent error bound for HL approximation, analogue of Thread 7 Corollary B but for π_h(x). **Cross-domain ingredient**: Hardy-Littlewood k-tuple conjecture (1923) + singular series. CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md status unchanged (singular series already USED-E in `sanity_singular_series.py`). **Cites** E1.5 (per-h sample-complexity argument), E6.x (sieve hierarchy primitive), S224 (Correlation Dichotomy template — NOT replicated for h-axis), S231 (Thread 6 P1 wrap — negative shape this slot matches in EXACT regime), S240-S244 (Thread 7 P3 — positive shape this slot matches in APPROX regime). See `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/{slot1_baseline.py, slot1_baseline_results.md, slot1_raw.tsv, slot1_samples.tsv}`, `archive/sessions/session